      "id": "claim_76610881b29040089c096f13ed9ec890",
      "statement": "consents-signal.ts exports four items: isBlocked() (returns boolean), setBlocked(next) (sets flag and notifies listeners), subscribe(listener) (registers callback, returns unsubscribe), and consentsOnError (onError handler that raises the flag when err.status === 451). It is a plain module with no React dependency, so consentsOnError can be passed to RhAuthProvider before any component renders.",
